Attached here [certificates.zip](https://github.com/caddyserver/caddy/files/14071812/certificates.zip) are the intermediate CA, client certificate and associated key files for ease of testing. The file client.p12 is provided in case either of you want to test a web browser, both Chrome and Firefox only support P12 files to the best of my knowledge. The certificate keys are plaintext. The certificates and associated keys were generated with the following commands, using Smallstep CLI: 

```bash
step-cli certificate create --insecure --no-password --not-after=175320h --profile=root-ca "Caddy Client CA Root CA" root.crt root.key
step-cli certificate create --insecure --no-password --not-after=175320h --profile=
intermediate-ca --ca ./root.crt --ca-key ./root.key "Caddy Client CA Intermediate CA" intermediate.crt intermediate.key 
step-cli certificate create --insecure --no-password --not-after=175320h --profile=leaf --ca ./intermediate.crt --ca-key ./intermediate.key "Caddy Client" client.crt client.key
step-cli certificate p12 --insecure --no-password client.p12 client.crt client.key
```
